tags: linux-syscalls-x86-64

The system calls that a process of an x86-64 guest can use, and their numbers: the
calls of Linux 6.12 for 64-bit processes. A kernel of a later version also gives them:
Linux does not remove or change a system call that processes use.

=== formal
behavior=the behavior of each call is the behavior of Linux 6.12 or of a later version of Linux
calls=the rows of the document 0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:da80dd0e7e4809297615e93a242849a073bc3b47fdcc404dd44223d0b8ecb044 whose second column is common or 64; the first column is the number of the call, the third column is its name
